recommend keep-going the arc now corrects a record, carries the correction, hears the answer, records the disagreement, escorts the word, bounds the objection, stands its standing, tells the raiser, reads their reply, carries a live quarrel past the run that heard it, makes the inheriting run answer for it, lets its holder close it, dates it, reads that age aloud, puts a long-standing one before a third hand, reads back what that hand made of it, makes the plan answer that finding on the record, carries the plan's own concession forward, makes the run that inherits it meet it, makes that meeting say what it found, carries that finding home to the reader who won it, and now reads what that reader makes of it -- so the question above is what a plan owes a reader who says the answer falls short: the word is read, published, and then nothing whatever follows from it, which means a supervisor may learn every run that its answer settled nothing and go on answering exactly the same way forever.
